  "scientific_reconciliation_note": "We evaluate both the Two-Stage Physical Concentration Model (predicting PM2.5 & PM10, then computing AQI deterministically) and Direct AQI Regression alongside Persistence. Both ML approaches achieve ~7.6-7.8 MAE, demonstrating that in high-autocorrelation environments, the Persistence baseline (MAE 7.42) remains an exceptionally tough benchmark to beat. We present these results transparently in the Forecast Arena without artificial exaggeration.",
  "model_comparison": [
    {
      "model_name": "Persistence Baseline",
      "description": "Predicts tomorrow's AQI equals today's AQI (AQI_t). Strong natural benchmark.",
